.TH "RTCPEERCONNECTIONICEERROREVENT.ERRORCODE" "3JS" "May 15, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent.errorCode \-
RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent: errorCode property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]errorCode\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent\f[R] interface represents the \c
.UR https://www.iana.org/assignments/stun-parameters/stun-parameters.xhtml#stun-parameters-6
STUN error code
.UE \c
\ returned by the STUN or TURN server if there was an error during ICE
negotiation.
.SH VALUE
A positive integer value stating the numeric \c
.UR https://www.iana.org/assignments/stun-parameters/stun-parameters.xhtml#stun-parameters-6
STUN error code
.UE \c
\ returned by the STUN or TURN server.
.PP
If no host candidate can reach the server, this property is set to the
number 701, which is outside the range of valid STUN error codes.
This value is reported only once per server URL, and only while the
\f[CR]iceGatheringState\f[R] is \f[CR]gathering\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example creates a handler for \f[CR]icecandidateerror\f[R] events,
which creates human\-readable messages describing the local network
interface for the connection and the ICE server used to attempt the
connection.
It then calls a function to display those messages and the value of the
event\(cqs \f[CR]errorCode\f[R] property.
.IP
.EX
pc.addEventListener(\(dqicecandidateerror\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] networkInfo = \(ga[Local interface: ${event.address}:${event.port}]\(ga;
  \f[B]const\f[R] iceServerInfo = \(ga[ICE server: ${event.url}]\(ga;

  showMessage(event.errorCode, iceServerInfo, networkInfo);
});
.EE
